   {
    "text": "I did not submit a candidate. The file has a plan code the contract doesn't list, and the profile doesn't show the value, so I can't tell a new plan from junk.\n\n- **What changed:** Six of 24 rows have a `plan_code` outside `[HMO, PPO, EPO, HDHP]`. The other 18 rows use only the listed codes. All other columns match the contract: same names, same order, no new or missing columns, and no empty values in required columns. `coverage_end` is empty on 18 rows, which its contract allows.\n- **Why I stopped:** The only fix that makes the file pass is adding the new code to `allowed`, and I'd have to guess its value to do that. Raising `max_bad_row_ratio` would also be a loosening the evidence doesn't support.\n- **Dry run on the current contract (unchanged):** the file is rejected. Accepted 0, rejected 6 (`VALUE.NOT_ALLOWED:plan_code` \u00d76), and `FILE.BAD_ROW_RATIO` fires because 25% is above the 5% limit.\n- **Next step:** someone needs to get the six unlisted `plan_code` values from the vendor or from the raw file. If they are a real new plan, I'll add that code to `allowed` in a new version. If they are junk, the file should go back to the vendor for a resend.\n\nAlso noticed, not changed: `member_id` is labelled as PHI in the profile but is not marked `phi: true` in the contract. Under the drift rules I leave existing columns' PHI settings alone, so this needs a separate decision by the owner.",
    "type": "text"
   }
